# docs/: only the documentation meant for readers is published. The proposal, the plans and
# schedules, the demo and readiness notes and other working papers stay on the author's machine.
# To publish another file, add a "!" line for it. A folder is listed with "/*" (not "/") so that
# git still looks inside it, which is the only way a "!" line can re-include a file in it.
docs/*
!docs/handover.md
!docs/api-reference.md
!docs/candidate-notice.md
!docs/plan/
docs/plan/*
!docs/plan/engineer-note.md
!docs/plan/email-setup.md
!docs/plan/ai-provider-switch.md
!docs/plan/hosting.md
!docs/plan/claude-api-cost-estimate.md
!docs/spikes/
docs/spikes/*
!docs/spikes/ollama-benchmark.md
!docs/spikes/browser-findings.md
!docs/spikes/video-anchor.md

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
